// Évalon (Ch8, MAP_EVALON): the Bourg d'Évalon, the screenless village of role-players in the
// Vallée de la Résonance. contenu-jeu/chapitres/08-evalon.md §2.2: a natural cirque of dark red
// iron-ore walls, half-timbered oak houses with mossy tiled roofs, cobbled lanes, oil lamps, the
// factions' pennants (blue: Ordre de l'Aube, green: Compagnie du Chêne), the water mill driving a
// steam engine, the Taverne du Dé à Vingt Faces with its Pigeonnier, the Échoppe du Troc, the Forge,
// the Tour du Scribe, the Maison des Anciens, the Galeries' mine mouth, the Porte du Fer under the
// belfry and the fortified Citadelle at the top. No screen, no neon, no cable.
// Footprints keep the map's doors (one cell each, bottom middle): the Taverne 3x4 (22, 26), the
// Échoppe 3x3 (28, 26), the Forge 3x3 (32, 30), the Tour 3x5 (6, 20), the Anciens 5x3 (42, 22); the
// Citadelle's gate (25, 3) and the Galeries' mouth (3, 12) are walkable doorways, as Fallarbor's were.
// The buildings and props stand on the packed earth (`under: terre`). `pont` is the lowered
// drawbridge (METATILE_PONT in ch08_evalon.rs). `falaise` comes first: a 1x1 stamp of metatile 513
// or 524 would equal an extract layout (studio map hygiene).
